--TEST--
an added method or static method is reached only in a file that uses its block: a file without the `use` line gets the ordinary unknown-member error, and its help names the block and the `use` line to add — `rule:classes/an-extend-block-adds-members-to-a-type`
--FILE--
<?nvs
autoload 'Shop' from './shop';

use Core\Time\Date;

echo Shop\Report::today(), "\n";
echo Date::at(2026, 9, 19)->isBusinessDay() ? "yes" : "no", "\n";
echo Date::newYear(2026)->year(), "\n";
--FILE shop/Report.nvs--
<?nvs
namespace Shop;

use Core\Time\Date;
use Shop\BusinessDays;

final class Report
{
    public static function today(): string
    {
        return Date::at(2026, 9, 17)->isBusinessDay() ? "open" : "closed";
    }
}
--FILE shop/BusinessDays.nvs--
<?nvs
namespace Shop;

use Core\Time\Date;

extend Date as BusinessDays {
    public function isBusinessDay(): bool {
        return $this->day() != 19;
    }

    public static function newYear(int $year): Date {
        return Date::at($year, 1, 1);
    }
}
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0405]: `Core\Time\Date` has no method named `isBusinessDay`
%A
  = help: the `extend` block `Shop\BusinessDays` adds `isBusinessDay`. Write `use Shop\BusinessDays;` at the top of this file to call it

error[E0405]: `Core\Time\Date` has no member named `newYear`
%A
  = help: the `extend` block `Shop\BusinessDays` adds `newYear`. Write `use Shop\BusinessDays;` at the top of this file to call it

error: aborting due to 2 errors
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
